  <h2>Independent educational service</h2>
  <p>Child Savings Lab is an independent informational project. It is not a government website, financial institution, account trustee, broker, investment adviser, tax-return preparer, accounting firm, law firm, payroll provider, benefits administrator, or ERISA fiduciary.</p>
  <h2>No individualized advice or professional relationship</h2>
  <p>Content and tools provide general educational information only. They do not create an attorney-client, accountant-client, adviser-client, fiduciary, employment, benefits, or other professional relationship. Use official sources and appropriately licensed professionals for decisions.</p>
  <h2>No filing, account access, or transaction service</h2>
  <p>The site does not access IRS records, determine whether an auto account exists, claim or activate an account, submit Form 4547, open an account, accept contributions, move money, select investments, or contact an employer or trustee.</p>
  <h2>Calculator limitations</h2>
  <p>Eligibility and status outputs are preliminary educational interpretations, not government determinations. Growth outputs are mathematical illustrations based on assumptions and simplified timing. They are not predictions, tax calculations, offers, solicitations, guarantees, or recommendations. Actual returns, fees, taxes, eligibility, contribution timing, and account procedures may differ.</p>
  <h2>Accuracy, rule changes, and availability</h2>
  <p>We aim to use authoritative sources, but laws, temporary and proposed regulations, agency guidance, forms, and operational procedures can change. A verification date does not guarantee that every later development has been incorporated. The site may be corrected, changed, suspended, or unavailable without notice.</p>
  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You may use the site for personal or internal educational purposes. Do not misrepresent it as an official government or professional service; probe, disrupt, or overload it; bypass security controls; use it to collect sensitive information from another person; or reproduce it in a misleading context.</p>
  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>Unless otherwise identified, original site text, presentation, code, and branding are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Government publications and third-party materials remain subject to their own terms. No permission is granted to use government names or third-party marks as an endorsement.</p>
  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>Links to government agencies and other sites are provided for convenience and sourcing. Child Savings Lab does not control their content, availability, security, or privacy practices, and a link does not imply endorsement or partnership.</p>
  <h2>Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the test site is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of accuracy, completeness, fitness for a particular purpose, noninfringement, or uninterrupted availability. The final production terms must receive counsel review before stating an operator-specific limitation of liability.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>Material changes should be dated. Before production launch, this page must identify the operating entity, monitored legal contact, governing law, venue, and any dispute terms. Do not send a child’s name, SSN, birth date, address, tax information, or account number to this project.</p>
